From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] hvf: a line in qemu.log when a vCPU stands still (Mac memory, no core)

What: when macOS runs out of free memory, a vCPU thread can stay blocked in
hv_vcpu_run for seconds (a stage-2 page fault waiting while macOS decompresses
or swaps in guest RAM, or for a free page) while the other vCPUs run on. The
guest then logs RCU stalls, its watchdogs fire, and nothing on the Mac side said
why. Each vCPU thread now counts its hv_vcpu_run calls (one relaxed store before
and one after the call, odd while in the guest). The stall watchdog's thread,
when it wakes anyway (every 2 s at most), reads every vCPU thread's CPU time and
Mach state with thread_info(); a vCPU that is still in the same call, got no
CPU time since, and is uninterruptible (blocked in macOS's kernel) or runnable
(no Mac core) stands still. While one stands, the watchdog looks every 250 ms;
a vCPU idle in the guest's WFI (waiting) never counts. One line per episode of
1 s or more (and one at 10 s, then every 30 s while it lasts):
  OmacVM: stall: vCPUs 1, 2, 3, 8 stood still for about 58 s, blocked in
  macOS's kernel waiting for memory (Mac: 0.3 GB free, pressure normal; the
  VM holds 51 GB, 20 GB of it compressed by macOS)
  OmacVM: stall: vCPU 5 waited 2.1 s for a Mac core (the Mac's CPUs are busy:
  load average 30)
vCPU numbers are the guest's CPU numbers. When it started is taken from the
vCPU's CPU rate before (a vCPU mostly idle: the latest it can be), so a time is
within about 1 s, never longer than seen. No line while the VM is not running,
and none for a look that came more than 1 s late or after the Mac slept (App
Nap, QEMU stopped): times are CLOCK_UPTIME_RAW, which stops while the Mac sleeps.
logs/vm-stalls ($OMACVM_LOGS/vm-stalls, key=value lines, written in one rename
after each episode, all zeros from QEMU's start): stalls, longest_ms,
longest_cause, last_ms, last_cause, last_vcpus, last_at, last_vm_mb,
last_free_mb, last_compressed_mb, and the main loop's stalls of 2 s or more in
a GPU run: gpu_stalls, gpu_longest_ms, gpu_last_where (the Mac's call and the
frame of QEMU or virglrenderer that made it). OmacVM.app and omacvm check read it.
OMACVM_STALL_WATCHDOG=0 turns it off with the watchdog (no thread_info at all).
Why: the user's VM froze on 2026-10-28 (RCU stall of ~60 s on CPUs 1, 2, 3, 8,
"no word from the Mac for 15 s"); on the Mac mini at critical memory pressure
the same showed up as vCPU threads uninterruptible in hv_vcpu_run for 1.2-2.4 s
with the BQL free (tracks/vm-stall.md). The line names that at once.
Upstream: OmacVM only.
Test: app/runtime/Tests/vcpu/test-vcpu-stall.sh (the logic and text in
include/qemu/omacvm-stall.h against simulated vCPU threads: the mini's stall,
the user's 60 s, 300 random stalls, paging noise, idle, late wakes, pauses;
build time and CI); the mini's repro row (work/vm-stall/kit/run-cpu.sh).

